<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures trade 10 lots in steady mkt.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures trade 10 lots in steady mkt.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ten lots of March 1997 Australian wheat futures traded on Tuesday, with the contract falling 50 cents to A$171.00 a tonne on the trade.</p>
<p>Settlement prices in nearer-term contracts firmed slightly.</p>
<p>Daryl French of broker FIMAT Australia Ltd said that with the Chicago market closed overnight, Sydney Futures Exchange wheat lacked direction.</p>
<p>He described the Australian market as sporadic and with little interest.  </p>
